      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Vive Pro Eye doesn't have an SDK for in-game eye tracking, only driver eye tracking to reduce pixels in your peripherals and sharpen them where you are directly looking, this is mainly for optimization reasons especially since vive pro has the resolution boost. Once Vive or someone makes a Vive Pro Eye \"Vive Eye | SDK\" for unity and UE4 then vrchat could look into changing the way the eye tracking system works, and this would also be up to Unity to make an update that allows for this eye-tracking system to be changed to work as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
